# The run environment's DEPENDENCY SPEC is tracked: Project.toml + Manifest.toml
# pin the exact EarthSciAST / EarthSciIO / Reactant / solver stack the runners
# were validated against, and losing them has already cost real debugging time --
# the env silently pinned a STALE vendored EarthSciIO, so the gridded-output sink
# failed with `EarthSciIO.OutputVar not defined` until it was repointed at the
# sibling ../EarthSciIO checkout.
#
# NOTE the path-dep entries are ABSOLUTE and machine-specific; on another machine
# re-run the `Pkg.develop(path=...)` calls for the sibling checkouts rather than
# expecting the Manifest to resolve as-is.
run-model-jl/*
!run-model-jl/Project.toml
!run-model-jl/Manifest.toml

# Local build state. `deps/EarthSciIO-fixes` in particular is a stale vendored
# EarthSciIO snapshot predating the Zarr writer surface; the env no longer
# references it and it should not be resurrected.
run-model-jl/deps/
